From: Airtype downstream
Subject: [PATCH] chat : let qwen3-coder call tools when a response format is set

The Qwen3-Coder parser (also used by Qwen3.5, Qwen3.6, Nemotron Nano 3, and Granite 4.2) returns
a response-format-only parser whenever a JSON schema is present, even when tools are offered with
automatic tool choice. The tools never reach the grammar, so the model cannot call one: an agent
that sends tools plus a response format on every turn, as OpenAI-compatible clients do, only ever
gets a schema answer, with values invented instead of looked up.

With both present, the reply is now either one tool-call section or the response-format JSON,
after the optional reasoning. Free text before a tool call stays excluded, since it would escape
the schema. The grammar stays eager (0001-chat-keep-response-format-grammars-eager.patch), so the
schema still constrains a reply that calls no tool. The generic autoparser and the other
specialized parsers with a response-format branch have the same gap and are not changed here.

Upstream report: not yet filed.

Validated against llama.cpp b11201 on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti (CUDA 13.3). Through the
airtype desktop OpenAI-compatible facade with Bonsai 27B Q1_0 (Qwen3.6), a request with a
get_weather tool and a strict response format returned schema JSON with an invented temperature
before the patch and a get_weather tool call after it. The airtype-desktop-inference-sidecar suites
tools_plus_structured_output_can_call_a_tool_qwen35_4b and
tools_plus_structured_output_can_still_return_schema_json_qwen35_4b pass with it on Qwen3.5 4B.

Refreshed for b12332; upstream now keeps response-format grammars eager without patch 0001.

diff --git a/common/parsers/qwen3-coder.cpp b/common/parsers/qwen3-coder.cpp
--- a/common/parsers/qwen3-coder.cpp
+++ b/common/parsers/qwen3-coder.cpp
@@ -86,8 +86,10 @@
             reasoning = reasoning_extracted;
         }

+        const bool uses_tools = has_tools && inputs.tool_choice != COMMON_CHAT_TOOL_CHOICE_NONE;
+
         // Response format parser
-        if (has_response_format) {
+        if (has_response_format && !uses_tools) {
             // The answer must be bare JSON, so the think block is consumed even when it is not extracted
             if (supports_reasoning && !extract_reasoning) {
                 reasoning = reasoning_skipped;
@@ -96,7 +98,7 @@
         }

         // Tool call parser
-        if (has_tools && inputs.tool_choice != COMMON_CHAT_TOOL_CHOICE_NONE) {
+        if (uses_tools) {
             auto arg_close  = p.tool_arg_close(p.literal("\n</parameter>\n"));
             auto arg_string = p.rule("xml-arg-string",
                 p.ac(p.tool_arg_string_value(p.until("\n</parameter>\n")) + arg_close, "\n</parameter>\n"));
@@ -173,6 +175,12 @@
                 tool_call;

             auto calls      = inputs.parallel_tool_calls ? tool_call_first + p.zero_or_more(tool_call) : tool_call_first;
+            // A constrained reply either calls a tool or answers in the requested schema.
+            if (has_response_format) {
+                auto tool_calls = p.trigger_rule("tool-call-root", calls);
+                auto response = p.content(p.schema(p.json(), "response-format", inputs.json_schema));
+                return generation_prompt + (reasoning << p.choice({tool_calls, response}));
+            }
             auto tool_calls = p.trigger_rule("tool-call-root", p.repeat(calls, min_calls, 1));

             // The templates separate content from the tool calls with one or two newlines,
